  "question": {
    "text": "One of the monomer of Nylon 6,6 is an acid. How many <math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> groups are present in this acidic monomer."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2.00",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Nylon 6,6 is a polymer of adipic acid and hexa methylene diamine. <br/>Adipic acid <math><mover><mrow><munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover><mrow><munder><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></munder></mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mover><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow></mover></math>  <br/>It has <math><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> groups."
  }
